# Commit semver tags

Every commit message **must** include an explicit bump tag so releases are intentional:

| Tag | Effect |
|-----|--------|
| `(major)` | breaking / incompatible change |
| `(minor)` | new feature, backward compatible |
| `(patch)` | fix, perf, refactor, docs, chore, etc. |

## Format

```text
type(scope): <# if available> (major|minor|patch) summary
```

Examples:

```text
feat(api): #42 (minor) add pagination
fix(auth): (patch) handle expired token
refactor!: (major) drop legacy v1 routes
docs: (patch) clarify release flow
```

## Rules for the agent

- When creating or drafting commits, **always** include `(major)`, `(minor)`, or `(patch)` after the optional issue/PR `#` and before the summary.
- Include `#<number>` when an issue or PR number is available; otherwise omit it.
- Prefer `(minor)` for user-visible features, `(patch)` for fixes and non-feature work, `(major)` only for breaking changes.
- Do not rely on `feat:` / `fix:` alone — the bump tag is required even when conventional prefixes are used.
- Skip the tag only for automated `chore(release):` commits produced by CI.
